  Q: What documents do I need to open a bank account in India?
  A: To open a bank account in India, you must provide the following documents:

1. Aadhaar number (or proof of possession) OR another Officially Valid Document (OVD) or equivalent e-document.
2. PAN (Permanent Account Number) or Form No. 60 if you do not have a PAN.
3. Other documents related to your business or financial status as required by the bank.

These requirements ensure compliance with KYC (Know Your Customer) norms (Source: rbi_kyc_master_direction.md).
[2026-08-30T15:12:29] sources=dicgc_guide_to_deposit_insurance.md
  Q: My deposits are split across 3 branches of the same bank — are they insured separately?
  A: No, your deposits across the 3 branches of the same bank are not insured separately. They are aggregated, and the ₹5 lakh cap applies to the total amount across all branches. (Source: dicgc_guide_to_deposit_insurance.md)
