[2026-08-30T19:27:39] sources=Master_Circular_RBI.pdf#p29, Master_Circular_RBI.pdf#p3, Master_Circular_RBI.pdf#p72
  Q: What are rules of Issuing large number of cheque books?
  A: Banks may issue cheque books with a larger number of leaves (20/25) if a customer demands the same. They should also ensure that adequate stocks of such cheque books are maintained with all branches to meet customer requirements. Additionally, the issuance of a large number of cheque books should be done in consultation with the Controlling Office of the bank (Source: Master_Circular_RBI.pdf, page 29).
