[2026-08-30T19:28:30] sources=RBIOS01072026.pdf#p5, RBIOS01072026.pdf#p6, RBIOS01072026.pdf#p7
  Q: How do I escalate a complaint to the RBI Ombudsman, and is there a fee?
  A: To escalate a complaint to the RBI Ombudsman, you must first approach the concerned Regulated Entity. If you do not receive a reply within 30 days or within the time specified by RBI, NPCI, or Card Network guidelines, or if you are not satisfied with the response, you can file a complaint with the RBI Ombudsman.

There is no charge or fee for filing or resolving complaints under the RBI Ombudsman Scheme (RB-IOS, 2026). Complainants do not need to approach any third-party agency or pay any fee to file a complaint with the RBI Ombudsman (Source: RBIOS01072026.pdf).
[2026-08-30T19:28:31] sources=MD18KYCF6E92C82E1E1419D87323E3869BC9F13.pdf#p32, MD18KYCF6E92C82E1E1419D87323E3869BC9F13.pdf#p33, MD18KYCF6E92C82E1E1419D87323E3869BC9F13.pdf#p47, rbi_kyc_master_direction.md
  Q: What documents do I need to open a bank account in India?
  A: To open a bank account in India, you must provide the following documents:

1. Aadhaar number (or proof of possession) OR another Officially Valid Document (OVD) or equivalent e-document.
2. PAN (Permanent Account Number) or Form No. 60 if you do not have a PAN.
3. Other documents related to your business or financial status as required by the bank.

Additionally, if you are opening a 'Small Account', you will need to provide a self-attested photograph, and a designated officer of the bank must certify your signature or thumb impression in their presence (Source: rbi_kyc_master_direction.md, MD18KYCF6E92C82E1E1419D87323E3869BC9F13.pdf).
